commit e08ee11df02263540108b8f9ac26d54e40a7d1fc
Author: Craig Xu Chen <craigxchen@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Jun 4 22:51:56 2026 -0400

    Add thermal exchange + temperature-gated extraction
    
    Phase 1.5 U6: per-particle lumped heat conduction + ambient loss, with the
    dissolution k_T reading the evolving grain temperature so a cooler pour lowers
    late extraction.
    
    - extraction.wgsl: thermal_exchange gathers neighbors (both species) on the
      counting-sort grid, reads temperatures from a fresh chem_frozen snapshot, and
      writes only the T lane of live chem. Capacity-weighted pair heat
      q_ij = clamp(κ(T_j−T_i)dt, ±reduced-capacity equilibrium) is antisymmetric
      (q_ji = −q_ij), so Σ C_i·T_i is conserved even for unequal capacities;
      ΔT_i = Σq/C_i + ambient loss. C = effective_mass·specific_heat (water scales
      with f_w; wet grain includes absorbed water ρ·V_abs). Phase-aware T lane
      helpers (grain T at .z, water T at .y).
    - mod.rs: thermal_exchange pipeline + bind group (6 storage buffers); a second
      chem→chem_frozen snapshot after the dissolution passes (preserving the
      post-dissolution c/pools) + the thermal pass, reusing the already-rebuilt grid.
    - tests: enthalpy-conservation gate with deliberately unequal capacities,
      relaxation + ambient cooling toward t_amb, cooler-pour-lowers-extraction (R9).
      dry_grain test narrowed to the solute lanes (thermal legitimately evolves T).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

